{
  "_about": [
    "DACH foods that USDA SR28 lacks. Each food uses exactly one transparent method, recorded in 'src':",
    "  recipe: computed by scripts/build_food_db.py from the USDA SR28 ingredients listed below (grams, or ml",
    "          converted with the ingredient's USDA density) and a cooking yield: 'yield' = cooked weight / raw",
    "          weight, or 'yield_g' = cooked weight in g. Water lost in cooking is subtracted from 'water'.",
    "          Drinks ('unit': 'ml') are per 100 ml of the finished drink ('yield_ml', default: sum of the ml).",
    "          No vitamin retention factors are applied, so heat-sensitive vitamins may be slightly overestimated.",
    "  label:  typical per-100 g (or per-100 ml) values printed on common Austrian/German supermarket products,",
    "          rounded conservatively. 'carbsExclFiber' is the EU label value (carbohydrate without fibre);",
    "          the build adds fibre so 'carbs' means total carbohydrate like USDA's. 'salt' is converted to",
    "          sodium (salt / 2.5). Only simple products use this method.",
    "Ids ('nina:<slug>') are stable forever: never rename or reuse one. 'item' fields are for people only.",
    "'portions' uses the same syntax as data/food-catalog.tsv. 'atwater' records a reviewed deviation."
  ],
